==Latvian==
{{slim-wikipedia|lang=lv}}
[[File:Lager_beer_in_glass.jpg|thumb|200px|Alus]]

===Etymology===
From {{inh|lv|bat-pro|*alu}}, from {{inh|lv|ine-pro|*h₂elut-|t=bitter}}. A minority view considers the Latvian and Lithuanian terms to be ultimately [[borrowing]]s from {{cog|gem}}, via {{cog|prg|-}}. Cognates include {{cog|lt|alùs}}, {{cog|prg|alu|t=honey drink}}, {{cog|orv|олъ|t=strong drink}}, {{cog|bg|олови́на|t=beer yeast}}, {{cog|sl|ôl|t=beer}}|ol, {{cog|ang|ealu}}, {{m|ang|alu}}, {{cog|en|ale}}, {{cog|non|ǫl|t=beer; feast}}, {{cog|grc|ἀλύδοιμος|t=bitter}}.<ref>{{R:lv:LEV}}</ref>

===Pronunciation===
* {{lv-IPA|alus}}
* {{audio|lv|lv-riga-alus.ogg}}

===Noun===
{{lv-noun|m|3rd}}

# [[beer]] {{gloss|[[alcoholic]] [[beverage]] [[usually]] [[make|made]] with [[barley]] [[malt]] and [[hop]]s}}
#: {{uxi|lv|gaišais '''alus'''|lager|lit=light '''beer'''}}
#: {{uxi|lv|tumšais '''alus'''|dark '''beer'''}}
#: {{uxi|lv|mājas '''alus'''|home '''beer'''}}
#: {{uxi|lv|amatnieku '''alus'''|craft '''beer'''}}
#: {{uxi|lv|med'''alus'''|honey '''beer'''}}
#: {{uxi|lv|'''alus''' muca|'''beer''' barrel, keg}}
#: {{uxi|lv|'''alus''' kauss|'''beer''' mug}}
#: {{uxi|lv|'''alus''' darītava|brewery|lit='''beer''' making place}}
#: {{uxi|lv|'''alus''' rūpniecība|'''beer''' industry}}
#: {{uxi|lv|darīt, vārīt '''alu'''|to make (literally, “to do”), to brew (literally, “to boil”) '''beer'''}}
#: {{ux|lv|Jāņiem tika brūvēts '''alus''', un nu staigāja no mutes uz muti liela, zaļa māla krūze, putām pārsegta, rūgteni smaržīga dzēriena pilna|in midsummer '''beer''' was brewed, and then a big, green clay jug went from mouth to mouth, covered with foam and full of (that) bitter, aromatic drink}}

